<https://hexplain.io/ns/register/media-encoding#PackBits> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Byte-oriented run-length coding (TIFF 6.0 section 9): a signed control byte n copies n+1 literal bytes (0 <= n <= 127), repeats the next byte 1-n times (-127 <= n <= -1), or does nothing (-128)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/register/media-encoding#PackBits> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use as a controlled value or grouping in this register. Profiles bind the appropriate scheme and map their raw wire codes to concept IRIs; membership does not prescribe a wire code. Codec/algorithm concepts require any applicable variant, framing and parameter information from the profile."@en .
