<https://hexplain.io/ns/register/media-encoding#SGILogRLE> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "SGI's LogL run-length coding (TIFF compression 34676): each row stored as its high then low byte plane, each run-length coded; decodes to the 16-bit log-luminance codes, little-endian, as libtiff's SGILOGDATAFMT_16BIT returns them."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/register/media-encoding#SGILogRLE> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use as a controlled value or grouping in this register. Profiles bind the appropriate scheme and map their raw wire codes to concept IRIs; membership does not prescribe a wire code. Codec/algorithm concepts require any applicable variant, framing and parameter information from the profile."@en .
