<https://hexplain.io/ns/register/media-encoding#XZ> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The .xz container: one or more streams of LZMA2-filtered blocks with an integrity check (CRC32, CRC64 or SHA-256). menc:LZMA names the algorithm family, not this framing."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/register/media-encoding#XZ> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use as a controlled value or grouping in this register. Profiles bind the appropriate scheme and map their raw wire codes to concept IRIs; membership does not prescribe a wire code. Codec/algorithm concepts require any applicable variant, framing and parameter information from the profile."@en .
